body:
@deralmas Sure thing. Here you go:

[debug.log](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/23971159/debug.log)

Just opened the editor, hovered around a few of the file menu items, and then clicked on one of the sidebar dropdowns that also show the issue.

Here is mine too:
[debug.log](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/23971209/debug.log)


@madsbangh , I am using the `Godot Engine v4.5.1.stable.official` not from the arch repo (I want to control when to upgrade) if that makes any difference.

Hi, I've taken a look.

So, this is very weird. The main window is offset -37 pixels, which means outside it. Maybe hyprland is compensating and offsetting everything but even then, judging from the popup calls, it should place them _higher_, if anything.

There's also this weird artifact in the video:

<img width="416" height="156" alt="weird artifact" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/62538e76-c884-4193-a5e5-2b1f0f14edf5" />

It looks like they're _rendered_ lower than actually requested?

This is super weird.

I can only assume that this is some libdecor shenanigan? That'd be even weirder as we use its utilities for calculating the position of popups and whatever and, as I said, those look roughly correct, if not even higher that they should be, not lower.

I guess you could try disabling it from the code.

```diff
--- a/platform/linuxbsd/wayland/wayland_thread.cpp
+++ b/platform/linuxbsd/wayland/wayland_thread.cpp
@@ -4743,7 +4743,7 @@ Error WaylandThread::init() {
 	}
 #endif // SOWRAP_ENABLED

-	if (libdecor_found) {
+	if (libdecor_found && false) {
 		libdecor_context = libdecor_new(wl_display, (struct libdecor_interface *)&libdecor_interface);
 	} else {
 		print_verbose("libdecor not found. Client-side decorations disabled.");
```

> This does not occur for me on Godot 4.5.1 when enabling Wayland, but it does on the latest 4.6 dev 5 release.

I don't recally any big difference since then, but maybe the new embedding layer is doing something funky? I don't think it should, but it never hurts to try: does running the editor with `GODOT_WAYLAND_DISABLE_EMBEDDER=1` fix the issue? example:

```sh
GODOT_WAYLAND_DISABLE_EMBEDDER=1 path/to/godot path/to/project.godot
```
